[# decorative/decorative-image: an image that adds no meaning (a flourish, texture or divider illustration).

   The alt text is left empty on purpose, so screen readers skip it. If the image carries information use
   content/image with real alt text instead.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: fixed width honored, border radius ignored.
   - Gmail apps: fine. If images are blocked nothing meaningful is lost, by definition.
   - Dark mode: images are not recolored. #]
[[ c('content/image', { image: { src: data.src, decorative: true } }, { settings: { align: s.align, width: s.width, padding: s.padding, radius: s.radius, hideOnMobile: s.hideOnMobile, hideOnDesktop: s.hideOnDesktop } }) ]]
